      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "[Video Animation & Batch Frames Overlay Workflow]\n\nLoads a video file (.mp4, .webm, etc.) and composites a camera viewfinder overlay with a blinking REC indicator and advancing timecode.\n\n■ IMPORTANT: Node Order (Overlay Belongs Last):\n- If you use frame interpolation (RIFE / FILM) or upscalers, ALWAYS place RecFrameVideoOverlay AFTER them (right before Create Video / Save).\n- Placing interpolation or upscale after the overlay causes HUD text smearing and timecode desync.\n\n■ Automatic FPS Synchronization:\n- The 'fps' input pin of RecFrameVideoOverlay is directly wired to 'Get Video Components' (or your video model's FPS output).\n- Timecode progression and frame counting automatically match your video's native rate (Wan 16fps, MiniMax 24fps, etc.).\n\n■ Advancing Seconds (:SS) & SMPTE Frame Counter (:FF):\n- Select 'now_sec' or 'smpte (00:00:00:00)' under timecode_mode for dynamic frame-by-frame and second-by-second updates even in short clips.\n\n■ Video-Specific Parameters:\n- blink_red_dot_interval: 24\n  * Blinking interval in frames for the red dot REC marker.\n  * At 24 FPS, the dot toggles on/off every 24 frames (1.0 second).\n  * Layout remains rock-solid without shifting when the dot is unlit.\n- advance_timecode_fps: 24.0\n  * Fallback frame rate when the 'fps' input pin is disconnected.\n\n■ Real-Time Frame Preview:\n- 'Preview REC Overlay' directly below allows instant live preview of your overlay design without queuing a prompt.\n\n■ Video Save & Export:\n- Combines composited frames with original audio and FPS via 'Create Video' and saves the final result with 'Save Video'."
      ],
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
